 **Example: Filter headers when proxying to ServerResponse**
 
+> **WARNING — SSRF risk:** Never pass a user-supplied URL directly to `got.stream` (or any HTTP client) in a server-side context. Doing so allows attackers to probe internal networks, cloud metadata endpoints (e.g. `http://169.254.169.254/`), and localhost services. **You MUST validate the URL before making the request.** The example below shows the required validation: reject non-`https:` protocols and restrict the hostname to an explicit allowlist. Adapt the allowlist to your own requirements before deploying.
+
 ```js
